  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "A truck travels \\(\\dfrac{b}{6}\\) feet every \\(t\\) seconds. There are \\(3\\) feet in a yard. How many yards does the truck travel in \\(3\\) minutes?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\dfrac{b}{1080t} \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\dfrac{30t}{b} \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\dfrac{30b}{t} \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\dfrac{10t}{b} \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\dfrac{10b}{t} \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "First express the travel time in seconds so it matches the given rate. Three minutes is \\(3\\cdot60=180\\) seconds. Since \\(t>0\\) is the given time interval, the truck's rate is\n\\[\n\\frac{b/6}{t}=\\frac{b}{6t}\n\\]\nfeet per second. Its distance in \\(180\\) seconds is therefore\n\\[\n180\\cdot\\frac{b}{6t}=\\frac{30b}{t}\n\\]\nfeet. There are \\(3\\) feet in each yard, so divide by \\(3\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{30b}{t}\\div3=\\frac{10b}{t}.\n\\]\nThe truck travels \\(\\frac{10b}{t}\\) yards, choice E.",
